{"sequence":28,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T23:37:11.918880825Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-a8d59226","body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs`, after the comammox step (around line 270-275), `alk_budget` is not decremented by `comammox_alk_cost`, even though the code comment says \"Debit shared budgets for comammox\" and `do_budget` is properly decremented. This is inconsistent with the DO budget pattern. While currently harmless (NOB does not check `alk_budget`), if a future guild is inserted after comammox that also requires alkalinity-limited rate ceilings, it would see a stale `alk_budget` that overstates available alkalinity, allowing over-consumption. Add `alk_budget = (alk_budget - comammox_alk_cost).max(0.0);` after line 273 for consistency.","dedup_key":"8f1e19e6569660d2ab7ad14656c02d8402911599e51aeff8c1d903dad63d2cec","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":29,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T23:37:11.928158210Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e30f07ff","body":"`crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs:234-240` still loads on-disk saves with `serde_json::from_str::<SaveFile>()`, while the new schema checks and migration chain only run in `SaveFile::from_json` / `SaveFile::from_value` (`crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:86-176`). This means the TUI file-load path can still bypass version validation and migrations: a legacy save can fail before migration once a new required field is added, and a v2 save that omitted `stability_tracker` will be deserialized with default zeros and then reserialized back to the API instead of getting the reseeded baseline that `from_json` applies. Route disk loads through the migration-aware constructor, or make `SaveFile`'s `Deserialize` impl delegate to that path so every consumer gets the same behavior.","dedup_key":"ce0a9793427fddb70b5258afc6bf7f9b0d53a77ece2dcf452c692010816b0204","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
