{"sequence":43,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T00:00:45.702494300Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-5d8c9ede","body":"The `hatch_produces_juveniles` test in `crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs:110-137` is failing. After the branch's chemistry/nitrogen cycle changes, the test setup no longer maintains good enough water conditions for shrimp reproduction — TAN reaches 2.168 mg/L (toxic) and population drops from 10 to 2 adults with 0 juveniles. Either the test's water chemistry setup needs retuning (higher nitrifier biomass, more frequent water changes, or lower feeding) to match the updated simulation dynamics, or there is a regression in the nitrogen cycle that causes ammonia to accumulate excessively despite the already-boosted nitrifier params.","dedup_key":"e8b763628bbe358d7941ee90d2d54f13fb7c72bc243ecc6a25c49398db1642d4","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":44,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T00:00:45.711142695Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-6289fe3d","body":"Migration functions use an infallible signature `fn(&mut Value)` (save.rs:29). Future migrations planned for phases B7 (nitrogen pool renames), D2 (carbonate state), E1 (habitat state), and F2 (richer shrimp state) may need to report errors — e.g., when a required source field is missing or has an unexpected type during a rename/transform. Consider changing `MigrationFn` to `fn(&mut Value) -> Result<(), SimError>` now, while there are only two migrations to update (one is a no-op), rather than after more migrations accumulate. The current `migrate_v2_to_v3` already has silent early-returns on missing `state`/`water` that would be better served by returning an error.","dedup_key":"890073d8cdc1306c7f6469f0a0add7bdef9d84dd33299edd19b8160d5d2d0d01","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":45,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T00:00:45.719638233Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-e6606032","body":"Make the new pre-step validation in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:490-492` non-mutating. `enforce_invariants` currently normalizes state in place at `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:6-8`, `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:95`, `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:109-147`, and `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:212-215` before it reaches the new hard failures at `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:129` and `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:185-210`. As a result, `step_hours(1)` can return `InvariantViolation` while still modifying the live engine; for example, a state with `water.ph = 9.0` and `shrimp_assimilation_efficiency = 1.2` comes back with `water.ph` clamped to `8.5`. Validate against a clone or split pure validation from normalization so rejected steps leave state untouched.","dedup_key":"788455b6de110687afd390552c5887d8dec80a068ef109be308f120c646e36fb","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
