{"sequence":71,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T00:40:22.104459388Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-ceb38e20","body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs:78-80`, the `SchemaVersionTooOld` error message says \"save file version {actual} is too old; minimum supported version is {min_supported}\" but unlike `SchemaVersionTooNew` (which suggests \"upgrade the application\"), it gives no remediation guidance. Consider adding actionable text like \"re-create this save with a newer version of the application\" so users know what to do when they encounter a v1 save.","dedup_key":"71ad1eca8a169a3e9d832d89a686f51219de8df086c4ba30b11c39806aec258c","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":72,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T00:40:22.113076047Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-b65ff026","body":"Make `crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_population.rs:111-155` fully deterministic instead of relying on a lucky RNG draw. In the current setup, `hatch_success_base = 1.0` is still multiplied by condition, oxygen, temperature, stability, and mineral factors in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:420-447`, so the assertion only passes because seed `7100` happens to satisfy `rng.next_f64() < p_hatch`. Force `p_hatch` to 1.0 (or exercise a deterministic helper/path) so unrelated changes to RNG consumption or chemistry tuning do not randomly break this test.","dedup_key":"4facdde9b4465ab3b176b4abd865f2e3b18cdaba5343f44177a8538b11c178f3","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
