{"sequence":85,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T01:02:11.287563876Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-6-e15be02d","body":"`crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:172-184` and `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:350-361` currently treat “the `stability_tracker` field exists” as “the tracker baselines are valid.” That breaks real schema-2 saves created before tracker seeding was added: those payloads can serialize the `StabilityTracker::default()` sentinel values, and the load path preserves them unchanged instead of repairing them. After migration, `prev_temp_c`/`prev_ph`/`prev_gh_d`/`prev_do_mg_l` can still be out of sync with the migrated water state, so the first daily stability update reports a fake swing. In a repro with a schema-2 save taken immediately after tank creation, the file loads with `instability_index == 0` but jumps to `0.3` after the next 24-hour step solely from stale tracker baselines. Please detect/reseed this legacy-default tracker case (while still preserving valid historical trackers) and add a regression test for a v2 payload where the tracker is present but uninitialized.","dedup_key":"f8133193db9de629fdf57d4bca063851748519f7ef4e6e9b3c08f451a596c8bb","run_id":"run-20260327225238","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
